{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277213-a-few-questions-about-aura","id":1277213,"title":"A Few Questions About Aura","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-28T09:45:51-08:00","id":1277213,"title":"A Few Questions About Aura","content":"1. If you're in aura, can you use an aura charm combined with a charm of a different element? Technically activating the charm kicks you out of aura, but does it let you get the combo off first? For that matter, do charms that have a bonus effect when in aura, or can only be used in aura, get to be comboed with charms expending aura?<br /> <br /> 2. If you expend aura in a turn only using that element, do you get it right back at the end of turn, since you spent a turn using only that element?<br /> <br /> The answer to these might be obvious but I reread through and didn't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T10:01:52-08:00","id":1277215,"title":"","content":"1) Per page 163: &quot;An Aura Charm can\u2019t be used in the same instant with Charms of other elements, unless those Charms have the Balanced keyword&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) I believe Vance said that you do. This does mean that &quot;spend aura&quot; is a bigger cost for charms that you use outside your turn. In-turn charms it's more of a restriction on what you can combo together (can only spend it once, y'know?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T10:27:37-08:00","id":1277223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1277213-a-few-questions-about-aura?p=1277215#post1277215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Per page 163: &quot;An Aura Charm can\u2019t be used in the same instant with Charms of other elements, unless those Charms have the Balanced keyword&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) I believe Vance said that you do. This does mean that &quot;spend aura&quot; is a bigger cost for charms that you use outside your turn. In-turn charms it's more of a restriction on what you can combo together (can only spend it once, y'know?)</div> </div> </div> </div>For example, the Resistance Fire Signature Charm, Raging Fire-Dragon Spirit, cannot supplement a rush action that you supplement with the Athletics Fire Signature, Inescapable Blazing Advance, since you need to spend a Fire Aura for the Athletics Charm, and the Resistance Charm ends as soon as you lose your Fire Aura.<br /> <br /> Even when dealing with Charms that don't end when you lose an Aura, they might have effects that only work when you have the Aura; these Aura-enhanced effects also fail to apply to the effects of another Charm that spends an Aura.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are specifically designed to be incapable of using their best tricks together. It's what justifies giving them so much power in singular tricks.<br /> <br /> Put another way, they are granted so much power in individual Charms so that they don't have to rely on putting their best tricks together to get their maximum output.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T13:24:31-08:00","id":1277245,"title":"","content":"Ah damnit, I knew at least one of these questions had an obvious answer that I somehow glossed over, thanks guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}